\section{Not yet verified}{
The spec records these as open. They are listed rather than hidden:

\itemize{
\item Whether to split '|'-joined protein-group accessions before parsing: mzLib does not, so the verb does not either. Splitting is a grouping rule, and it belongs in mzLib if anywhere.
\item An isoform or version past int.MaxValue is dropped with no signal while the namespace still reads uniprot or refseq (ProteinAccession.NumberOrNull). Whether mzLib should leave such an accession unrecognized instead is an mzLib question, not raised upstream yet.
\item Not yet ported to mzLibRust or mzLibR; the binding names above are proposals.
}
}
